{
 "sub_strand": "MATH.G7.MEASUR.AREA",
 "title": "Area",
 "status": "draft: written 17 Nov 2026 offline for the Grade 7 pilot; not yet checked by a Kenyan maths teacher; not loaded by the live tutor",
 "sources": [],
 "notes": "Official outcomes a to d are tested; e is an attitude. 1 m2 = 10,000 cm2 (100 x 100); 1 hectare = 10,000 m2; the acre is given in the question (about 4,000 m2), since it is not a metric unit. Parallelogram and rhombus: base x perpendicular height (a rhombus also half the product of its diagonals); trapezium: half the sum of the parallel sides x height; circle: pi x r x r with pi = 22/7. Borders are the outer shape minus the inner one. Grade 5 found rectangles by counting and by length x width; Grade 6 did triangles, combined shapes and estimated circles by counting squares.",
 "skills": [
  {
